      "The description is a routing trigger. State concrete situations when to load the skill and when not to load it. Include task vocabulary, boundary cases, and exclusions. Keep procedural detail in the body, loaded only after selection. Pi advertises names and descriptions before loading full instructions; use a SKILL.md directory for portability. Names are lowercase, hyphen-separated, at most 64 characters. Descriptions are at most 1024 characters. References use paths relative to the skill directory. Review unfamiliar instructions and supporting files before trusting them.\nRed authoring contract: provide whenToUse, whenNotToUse, useExamples, avoidExamples, sources, evidenceRunIds, positive and negative cases, and concise procedural instructions. Avoid one-off facts, credentials, private thinking, or instructions to expand permissions. Proposals are inert data. A passing keyword trigger test checks consistency only, not whether the model will select the skill or perform better. Held-out observed outcomes and owner review are necessary to claim improvement. Active descriptions may be advertised; full bodies should be loaded only on demand. Skills cannot grant access or authorize actions. A skill is not executable code or a host policy override.",
