    content:
      "TeleTune edits a textual library while leaving model weights unchanged. It learns from successful logged trajectories, separated into train and development sets. Teacher forcing restores recorded actions after wrong predictions. The optimizer proposes bounded edits from prediction errors; candidates replace the baseline only when development-set action-prediction accuracy improves. Workflows encode reusable procedures; skills resolve specific decisions. Retrieval chooses demonstrations covering complementary task subgoals.\nFor Red: runtime telemetry is evidence, not automatically a successful demonstration or independent ground truth. Keep session/run attribution, source provenance, failures, quota and latency. Never log credentials, tool payloads, or private reasoning. Propose immutable skill revisions from attributable evidence. Test positive and negative trigger cases, clearly mark them as smoke tests, and do not claim this is the paper's full evaluation. Independent held-out replay/prediction evaluations require a separate evaluator with trusted labels. Owner-reviewed activation and rollback remain separate from model-accessible proposal tools. Record rejected revisions to avoid repeating them. The offline proxy and benchmark results are not a guarantee of performance for this personal agent.",
